  "notes": "Sheet-metal angle bracket in millimeters, material plain carbon steel. Third-angle-style drawing interpreted as front/back plate with Ø82 through opening, two horizontal feet with Ø12 through holes, and two sloped side webs. Model is an approximate multibody sheet-metal representation using 3 mm default wall thickness. Several formed/bent surfaces, R5 inside bend radii, R7 outside corner radii in 6 places, R30 side transition, and 37 degree side profile are recorded as dimensions/notes but approximated with rectangular plates because exact non-rectangular side plate polygon and bend geometry are not fully encoded. The top/front view shows a 100 mm wide by 8 mm deep rounded rectangular top opening/slot with 70 mm internal straight span; approximated by the open U-shaped bracket/plate layout rather than a separate cut. Small foot hole z positions estimated as 25 mm from the front edge based on the 25 mm dimension in the top view; x positions set 35 mm from each outer side, symmetric about centerline. Overall bounding box assumed X=116 width, Y=105 height, Z=100 depth."
